                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "We’ve made it to Christmas Puzzle 2 and immediately there are noticeable changes. It’s easier to match pieces, the way logic or luck works is much more in the player’s favour. You get 2 power ups instead of 1 and both are very powerful. Having them around will influence the outcome more effectively. Because of this, you don’t have to grind as much because you need fewer of them. The timer is generally more generous even if there still might be a few tight ones. You don’t need to get 3 stars for an achievement but even so, they’re not as difficult to get. You can even turn off the timer at any time.\n\nThose are all needed changes to have a fairer balance but I am also disappointed about a few things. The music is copied from the first game with no changes.  I didn’t notice it early but I’m certain puzzles from 1 were copied and remixed to make them fairer with a new paint etc, definitely the ones from chapter 2 and 3. I also experienced something bizarre. Upon starting the game, a bunch of achievements unlocked and I’ve already made progress somehow. My save file from Christmas Puzzle 1 is compatible with 2, that seems to be causing this problem. I decided to start on a new file to play like a first timer would. I’ve spent 6 hours and made it up to chapter 3. I skipped chapter 4 since the achievement unlocked automatically for it and a lot of puzzles will probably be copied from the first game. Although it’s good that you can turn the timer off, you can still see the stars greyed out. You get none by default which feels bad, I’d have preferred not seeing the stars anymore.\n\nI’m a bit mixed about CP2. I had a better time, the balance is fairer than before and some lessons were learned. But I’m unhappy with some of the things I mentioned,  I don’t know if I’d go as far to say that it shows a bit of lazy effort since copying levels and using the same music is very blatant. There is no question that 2 is the better game and it should be the starting point for the franchise. Newcomers won’t notice or care about most of the issues if they haven’t played 1. Looking at its own merits, 2 is a pretty good game but it’s nothing you haven’t seen before. Still, you can play it and have a good time if you’re looking for the next match 3 puzzle fix. This one is easier to recommend on a decent sale or with a bundle.",
